nceClasses, toolComponents)\n2867\t\t\t\tif toolEv == \"\" && len(tool.EvidenceClasses) == 0 {\n2868\t\t\t\t\t// A tool that declares no evidence class does not report a\n2869\t\t\t\t\t// validation result at all — `artifact-check` and `review-check`\n2870\t\t\t\t\t// are POSE commands, and what supports their disposition is that\n2871\t\t\t\t\t// the command ran. Naming the tool is a real reference to that;\n2872\t\t\t\t\t// reaching for an unrelated sealed result, as this used to, said\n2873\t\t\t\t\t// nothing about whether the tool ran.\n2874\t\t\t\t\ttoolEv = \"check:\" + tool.ID\n2875\t\t\t\t}\n2876\t\t\t\tif toolEv == \"\" {\n2877\t\t\t\t\t// The same invention the criteria path stopped doing one spec\n2878\t\t\t\t\t// ago, on the other half of the attestation: `validation:auto-\n2879\t\t\t\t\t// attest`, `<class>:auto-attest`, `docs:auto-attest` — none of\n2880\t\t\t\t\t// them pointing at anything, and nothing downstream checking.\n2881\t\t\t\t\t// The distinction between a judged review and a stamped one\n2882\t\t\t\t\t// does not survive one half of it being fabricated.\n2883\t\t\t\t\tif requiresEvidence {\n2884\t\t\t\t\t\tif len(tool.EvidenceClasses) > 0 {\n2885\t\t\t\t\t\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review tool %s requires evidence class %s and bundle %s seals none; run the tool, or record its disposition with `pose review attest --tool`\", tool.ID, strings.Join(tool.EvidenceClasses, \"|\"), bundleID)\n2886\t\t\t\t\t\t}\n2887\t\t\t\t\t\treturn ReviewAttestation{}, nil, fmt.Errorf(\"pose: review tool %s has no evidence in bundle %s; run the tool, or record its disposition with `pose review attest --tool`\", tool.ID, bundleID)\n2888\t\t\t\t\t}\n2889\t\t\t\t\t// `deferred`, not `not-used`: a required tool recorded not-used\n2890\t\t\t\t\t// is a blocker whatever the reason, while a deferral is the\n2891\t\t\t\t\t// disposition the engine already accepts for a tool whose\n2892\t\t\t\t\t// precondition this scope cannot meet.\n2893\