{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgnH4skvScEACmA2qkUnk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Decision: approved.** This round only corrects the typed form of the previous draft. It uses the source review I already did on df7da2f0, and Bash was denied again, so I ran no tests or `pose` commands myself.\n\n**Checks made for this correction**\n- **Native rules:** the rules the notes cite exist at `pose-mcp/internal/pose/review_bundle.go:2840-2902`. A tool with the `review-complete` precondition is `deferred`. A component whose producer coverage is `none` is `not-used`. A recommended tool may be `not-used`. A required tool that declares no evidence class uses `check:<tool-id>`.\n- **Canonical validation:** `.pose/results/delivery-validation.json` records 189 passed and 0 failed, but against `git_head` 4054d6be, not df7da2f0. The notes say df7da2f0 is an administrative checkpoint with no source change. I couldn't diff the two commits to confirm that, so the validate rationales below say so.\n\n**Round-1 findings**\n- **R1-F1:** fixed.\n- **R1-F2:** fixed.\n- **R1-F3:** not fixed, carried as the owned follow-up F3 (owner `@pose-maintainers`, review by 2026-12-06).\n\n**Tool results I did not see run**\n- `artifact-check` and `knowledge-check` are marked passed using the engine's own `check:<id>` reference to the primary run's execution. I did not run either one or check its output.\n- `surface-check` and `assess-integrate` are marked passed on sealed integration records. Their actual command results come from the primary run, not from my session.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\n  \"schema\": \"pose.review.draft/v1\",\n  \"decision\": \"approved\",\n  \"findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"F3\", \"severity\": \"low\", \"disposition\": \"follow-up\", \"file\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/index_generation_build.go\", \"line\": 205, \"summary\": \"Index build failure code 'federated-roadmap' is still selected by substring match on error text instead of a typed/sentinel error; recorded as an owned open follow-up in the spec.\", \"action\": \"Replace the substring classification with a typed error while preserving the code, receipts and negative controls.\", \"owner\": \"@pose-maintainers\", \"review_by\": \"2026-12-06\"}\n  ],\n  \"prior_findings\": [\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F1\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go:388-408 merges the authorized-root registry audit into perRoot[op.primary], which metadata (:438-538) consumes, so freshness/limitations/ID reflect it; changed/conflict are 'changed' (retry once), budget exhaustion is 'unknown' only. Regressions pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view_d7_probe_test.go:225-375 cover review, closeout and projection for stable/once/changed/conflict/budget; sealed integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration pass.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F2\", \"status\": \"fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/pose/governance_read_view.go:2074-2078 shares immutable captured bytes after capture closed and readers joined; caller isolation is preserved by copies at :1423, :1508 and :1522.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"R1-F3\", \"status\": \"not-fixed\", \"evidence\": \"pose-mcp/internal/cli/index_generation_build.go:205 unchanged; owned open follow-up at .pose/specs/2026-10-13-pose-governance-read-view-generation.md:409 (owner @pose-maintainers, crit low, review 2026-12-06); carried as current finding F3.\"}\n  ],\n  \"sweep\": \"Source review of df7da2f0 (read-only; Bash for git/go test/pose was denied in every session of this review, so no command was executed by me): operation final audit, metadata and per-root audit (governance_read_view.go:346-538), readFile/open caller isolation and budgets (:1414-1530), audit byte reuse (:2074-2146), obligation projection retry/coverage and reason classifier (obligation_projection.go:136-358, 838-848, 962-1010), review/closeout read-view retry and application (review_closeout.go:450-620), index capture/retry and publication under the guard (governance_read_view_capture.go, cli/index_generation_build.go), write guard, lock paths and scoped guard (governance_write_guard.go, governance_scoped_write.go, spec_transfer_locks.go), action write scope (action_write_scope.go:1-120), D9 executable digest (review_run_provenance.go:221-255), new registry regressions (governance_read_view_d7_probe_test.go:202-375), .pose/policy/delegation.json and its distpolicy exclusion, POSE.md/ADR budget documentation, validation matrix entry, and the native attestation rules (review_bundle.go:2840-2902). Observation, not a defect: .pose/results/delivery-validation.json records git_head 4054d6be (189 passed, 0 failed) while the bundle head is df7da2f0, described as administrative only. No new defects found.\",\n  \"criteria\": [\n    {\"id\": \"assumption-integrity\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a47effa4f8e59c51\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the spec constraints, the A->B->A paragraph, the ADR budgets and the follow-up list. Verified facts: captured-byte identity, final audit, single retry and guarded writes exist in source (governance_read_view.go, governance_write_guard.go). Accepted risks are explicit: uncooperative external writers/ABA are outside the guarantee, no universal filesystem transaction is claimed, and F3 is owned until 2026-12-06. Unresolved limits are kept rather than hidden: tech-debt INCOMPLETE (two historical specs unreadable), the prior global structural check on b7b5680f is not relabelled current, and my own session could not execute commands. Conclusion: assumptions are separated correctly from verified facts.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-concurrency\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The sealed check runs with -race over the pose, cli and mcpserver read-view, guard and index selections. In source, view reads serialize on v.mu, the audit waits for active readers (governance_read_view.go:2049-2053), operation budgets use budgetMu, and the write lease uses atomic plus once-release with canonical root ordering (governance_write_guard.go:78-187, 472-528).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-contracts\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\", \"rationale\": \"ObligationReport stays schema v1 with an additive read_view object (schema v1); review and closeout add an optional read_view field (review_closeout.go:420-430); the MCP catalog golden documents read_view. CLI/MCP result parity is covered by the sealed check.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-input-errors\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/typed-diagnostics-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Guard refusals are typed sentinels wrapped in GovernanceWriteGuardError without host paths (governance_write_guard.go:23-65). Read-view failures use ErrGovernanceReadViewChanged/Unknown with clipped, bounded summaries (governance_read_view_capture.go:88-137), and index build failures map to stable codes. F3 is the remaining low-severity untyped classification.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-integration-impact\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Projection, review, closeout, index build and writers all consume the same view/guard primitives across the pose, cli and mcpserver packages; the sealed integration selection covers these boundaries.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"backend-observability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Limitations name the producer and reason, changed paths are root-relative display paths, roots are exposed as digests, and error summaries are capped at 8 producers, 4 reasons and 2048 bytes (governance_read_view_capture.go:88-137).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"compatibility\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-mcp-operation-results-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Examined the report and Obligation schema versions (both remain 1), the additive read_view, the documented treatment of legacy reports without a binding as readable but non-authorizing (POSE.md:372), and the MCP catalog descriptions. Historical records are not rehashed. Conclusion: compatible, with the additions explicitly documented.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"correctness\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R1-F1 is fixed: the registry final audit reaches metadata, so review, closeout and projection report unknown and do not keep approval or terminal status on a change (governance_read_view.go:388-408; regressions in governance_read_view_d7_probe_test.go:225-375). Positive controls (stable, recovered once) remain current.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"cross-component-integration\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/cli-profile-parity-integration\", \"rationale\": \"CLI and MCP surfaces consume the same domain projection and review evaluation; sealed parity checks pass.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"design-causality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a47effa4f8e59c51\", \"rationale\": \"Root cause per the spec: CurrentObligationSnapshot did not bind journal/subject bytes and the closure was not audited after the producers ran. D2 extends Files with per-operation capture that serves the same bytes to every producer; the final audit plus one retry addresses R3; D3 makes the disclosure additive; D4 guards writers per root with B14 CAS for R6/R7; D5-D7 bound budgets and per-scope views from measured corpora; D8 and D9 address instance policy and the executable-hash bound. The structure check passed.\", \"mappings\": [\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-0cf58a00\", \"basis\": \"R10\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The validation matrix adds the required race check governance-read-view-integration over the B34 test selection and explicit -count=1 build/test/vet checks, qualifying R10's fixtures and fault injection as Validation V7 requires.\"},\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-5c5ba300\", \"basis\": \"D2\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"The spec constraint requires the B34 ADR to be accepted before the contract changes; the ADR records the bounded operation-scoped view and its budgets on which decisions D2-D9 rest.\"},\n      {\"delta\": \"SD-98ca1442\", \"basis\": \"D8\", \"disposition\": \"mapped\", \"rationale\": \"delegation.json is instance-only configuration of the independent-review agents and is excluded from the embedded scaffold (distpolicy.go:115-118), as D8 decides. Its narrowed session regex responds to the retained capture failure rrn-db41024e48aa50af. It contains no secrets.\"}\n    ]},\n    {\"id\": \"documentation\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a47effa4f8e59c51\", \"rationale\": \"POSE.md:372-373 (and its pt-BR and scaffold copies) describe snapshot.read_view, the ID binding, separate coherence/coverage/freshness, 'current' meaning only the final audit instant, legacy non-authorization and the budgets; the ADR documents 25,000 records, 512 MiB, 8 MiB and 16 roots; the MCP catalog descriptions mention read_view freshness and limitations. They match the runtime behaviour I read.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"milestone-exit-gate-pose-state-consistency-and-recovery-governance-read-view\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"Captured bytes, entries, links and errors define the ID (metadataSingle); mtime and identity are included, so even same-size edits change it. Interleaving triggers one retry, then coherent=false/unknown with incomplete coverage, and the registry path no longer relabels a changed view as current (R1-F1 fixed). Coverage loss blocks Complete (obligation_projection.go:341-348). Effects revalidate under the per-root guard with B14/B15 CAS (start.go, action_request.go, index_generation.go). External-writer and A->B->A limits are explicit. There is no inter-operation cache.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"operability\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a47effa4f8e59c51\", \"rationale\": \"Index failures say whether anything was written and tell the user to rerun `pose index` or `pose index --verify` (cli/index_generation_build.go:39-117); guard busy/unavailable errors name the operation and root label; read-view limitations name producer and reason. F3 does not hurt the user-visible message, only how it is classified.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"requirements\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"R1-R10 are exercised by the sealed B34 race selection plus the obligation-projection, writer-publication, index-generation and state-attention checks; the R3/R5 registry interleaving gap from round 1 now has dedicated regressions.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"scope\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a47effa4f8e59c51\", \"rationale\": \"Compared the change list with the spec's artifact plan: every changed source and governance file is declared, and the instance delegation policy is covered by D8. No watcher, daemon, global cache, B31/B33/B35 work or host adoption was added, matching the plan's exclusions.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"security\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a47effa4f8e59c51\", \"rationale\": \"Lock directories and the lock file are checked against symlink, non-regular and escape substitution, with SameFile confirmed after open (governance_write_guard.go:437-548). Foreign writes require explicit root bindings and the exact project set (governance_scoped_write.go:68-98). Outputs use root digests, not absolute paths. The executable digest checks the regular file, opened identity and bounded size (review_run_provenance.go:225-255). The live delegation policy is not shipped (distpolicy.go:118). No secrets were found.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"solution-proportionality\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a47effa4f8e59c51\", \"rationale\": \"The smallest sufficient alternative, re-hashing a few named files, would not bind directory listings, errors or federated roots, and would not prevent mixed producer results; the chosen design extends the existing Files seam with no daemon or cache. Cost: per-read mutex serialization and retained bytes up to the measured 512 MiB budget (no longer doubled after R1-F2). The choice would be invalidated if real corpora outgrew the D6 budgets without a new measurement, or if B35 runtime caching were adopted.\"}\n  ],\n  \"tools\": [\n    {\"id\": \"artifact-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"check:artifact-check\", \"rationale\": \"Required tool with no evidence class, so the engine's reference is the command execution. The primary execution ran it successfully on the current source before sealing; I did not run it myself (Bash denied) and could not inspect its output, so I am relying on the recorded execution and not on my own run.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-design\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"structure:design-a47effa4f8e59c51\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed structural design result passes for this bundle.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; not executed in my restricted session and no sealed result exists for it.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-discover\", \"component\": \"tests\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; not executed in my restricted session and no sealed result exists for it.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-integrate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The primary execution ran assess integrate on the current source; its inventory is static, not functional proof. The cited sealed integration record is the passing evidence of the class the tool requires. I did not run the command myself.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"assess-tech-debt\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; not executed by me. The known limitation stands: the scan is INCOMPLETE because two historical specs cannot be read, and it is not claimed as complete.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"closeout-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Post-review gate: this tool has the review-complete precondition and can only run meaningfully after this review's conclusion is recorded.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"knowledge-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"check:knowledge-check\", \"rationale\": \"Required tool with no evidence class. The primary execution ran it successfully before sealing; I did not run it myself (Bash denied) and am relying on that recorded execution.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"review-check\", \"disposition\": \"deferred\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Post-review gate: this tool has the review-complete precondition and evaluates the review state this conclusion produces, so it runs after attestation.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; not executed in my restricted session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"suggest-review\", \"component\": \"tests\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"Recommended tool; not executed in my restricted session.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"surface-check\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"integration:pose-mcp/go/spec-surface-integration\", \"rationale\": \"The primary execution ran surface-check on the current source with zero findings; the cited sealed integration record is the passing evidence of the required class. I did not run the command myself.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"The canonical global matrix result in .pose/results/delivery-validation.json records 189 passed and 0 failed with git_head 4054d6be (the source-correction commit); df7da2f0 is described as an administrative checkpoint, which I could not diff-verify. The sealed records cite that validation. This is not the prior b7b5680f structural check.\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"pose-mcp\", \"disposition\": \"passed\", \"evidence\": \"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\", \"rationale\": \"Sealed pose-mcp module checks pass: build, the full uncached test suite and the B34 race integration (integration:pose-mcp/go/governance-read-view-integration).\"},\n    {\"id\": \"validate\", \"component\": \"tests\", \"disposition\": \"not-used\", \"evidence\": \"\", \"rationale\": \"The validation matrix declares this component runs no check (replaceDefaultChecks with an empty list, producer coverage none), so no producer can emit evidence for it.\"}\n  ]\n}\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":215,"cache_read_input_tokens":197320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":215},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"be9c63b9-4284-44e8-8085-926efcf2b108","timestamp":"2026-11-06T20:08:23.157Z","request_id":"req_011CgnH4sZGMf37Q7djtD7D8"}
